                <pb facs="0107" n="79" xml:id="pg79"/>

                <head>31. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>A meeting to discuss differing views on the best way to proceed with the
                    paramilitary operation against Cuba was convened at the White House on February
                    18, 1961. According to summary notes of the meeting, CIA Deputy Director for Plans Richard Bissell outlined the status
                    of planning and preparation, following which the group discussed how to generate
                    support for the operation and other matters. Ambassador Bohlen expressed the view that the USSR would not react if the operation were
                    finished quickly but might react if it dragged on. For text of the notes, see
                        <ref target="frus:frus1961-63v10/pg_108"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations</hi>, 1961–1963, volume X, page 108</ref>.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
